e Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/oklahoma/pittsburg-county"],["ARC or PLC in Pittsburg County","/arc-plc/oklahoma/pittsburg-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Pittsburg County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years. In 2025 that same pair came in at 41% of normal, after April to May hit 182%. So far in 2026, June to July stands at 121% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 17838 had its driest year in 1963 at 50% of normal.</p>"}
